A KMS device with no render node (the apple KMS device on Asahi, evdi for
DisplayLink docks) means aquamarine can never create its secondary renderer for
it. On hotplug, SDRMConnector::connect() bails out on that failure before
emitting the output, so a monitor plugged in after Hyprland starts is never
shown. At startup (recheckOutputs) and on applyCommit the same failure is only
logged, and rendering works fine without it, so do the same here.

That renderer is also retried on every applyCommit, and each attempt logs five
lines (EGL probe + errors): at 60 Hz that is the whole of a 3 GB hyprland.log in
a few days. Skip the attempt when the device has no render node; the renderer
is only ever used to blit for secondary GPUs of this backend.
--- a/src/backend/drm/DRM.cpp
+++ b/src/backend/drm/DRM.cpp
@@ -641,6 +641,11 @@
         if (rendererState.renderer && rendererState.allocator)
             return true;
 
+        // no render node: initMgpu can never succeed, and this renderer is only
+        // needed to blit for secondary GPUs. Don't retry (and log) on every commit.
+        if (gpu->renderNodeFd < 0)
+            return true;
+
         return initMgpu();
     }
 
@@ -1686,10 +1691,8 @@
     if (!backend->backend->ready)
         return;
 
-    if (!backend->updateSecondaryRendererState()) {
+    if (!backend->updateSecondaryRendererState())
         backend->backend->log(AQ_LOG_ERROR, std::format("drm: Failed to update renderer state for {} on connect", szName));
-        return;
-    }
 
     auto primaryBackend = backend->primary ? backend->primary : backend;
     output->swapchain   = CSwapchain::create(backend->backend->primaryAllocator, primaryBackend.lock());
